    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d100">

                <pb facs="0193" n="113" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg113"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bryan to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-27"><hi rendition="#italic">September 27,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 455.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm my
                        telegram<anchor n="a" xml:id="d100-f1"/> of September 27, and the
                    satisfaction to state that through the good offices of the governor of Rio
                    Grande do Sul, which I had sought, the heirs of Baron Thomsen have effected a
                    final arrangement with the State as to the terms of payment of their inheritance
                    tax. I inclose herewith a letter from the American consular agent at Rio Grande
                    do Sul reporting the amicable closing of the case.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Page
                    Bryan.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d100-a1.xml" xpointer="d100-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
